menu "Tab5X test options"

config TAB5X_DRIVER_SMOKE_TEST
    bool "Run camera and audio driver smoke tests at boot"
    default n
    help
        After normal startup, run one audio record/playback cycle and capture
        camera frames for five seconds. This validates driver calls and data
        movement only; it does not assess acoustic or image quality.

config TAB5X_AUDIO_I2S_DIAGNOSTICS
    bool "Enable audio I2S transfer diagnostics"
    default n
    help
        Collect and print board-level audio TX full-write, I2S timing, frame-gap,
        retry/error, and internal/DMA/PSRAM heap statistics. The full-write
        behavior remains active when this option is disabled; only the added
        diagnostic counters and periodic logs are removed.

config TAB5X_MP3_DECODE_DIAGNOSTICS
    bool "Enable MP3 decode diagnostics"
    depends on AUDIO_PLAYER_ENABLE_MP3
    default n
    help
        Collect and print MP3 input refill, sync search, Helix decode, decoder
        call-gap, output-byte, error, heap, and buffer-memory-location statistics.
        A first-frame report and cumulative reports at about five-second intervals
        are emitted. Disable this option for normal operation to remove the timing
        and diagnostic log overhead.

endmenu
